rsx draw engine + texture layout: shadow maps are read as depth and get a depth target; full surface/zeta tables evict.

Resistance 3 had no shadows from its lamps (the Home level: no shadow of the table or the people under the hanging
lamp). A probe in the light shader (scratch only) showed the depth it read from every shadow map was exactly 0. Two
causes, both needed for the shadows to come back:
- The light shaders read the Z16 shadow maps as DEPTH16 through crossbar 0xA900: R, G and B from source A.
  rsx_texture_component_remap mapped the depth formats like A8R8G8B8, so A was the decoded resource's opaque alpha
  and every shadow compare saw depth 1.0. The depth formats (0x90..0x93) now present their one channel on every
  source, as RPCS3 maps them (VKFormats.cpp get_component_mapping: R,R,R,R).
- g.surfaces and g.zdepths hold 64 entries each and nothing ever left them. By the time Home loads, the prologue's
  and cutscenes' targets fill both, so the level's eleven shadow maps (rendered once at load, at 0x01EB1000,
  0x01FB9800, ...) got no depth target: eng_zdepth_get returned ENG_INVALID, they were rendered without depth and
  read back from guest memory as zeros. A full table now gives up the entry used longest ago (bound, sampled or
  presented), never one used this frame or the last nor the last presented surface; with nothing older the caller
  gets no slot, as before. What an evicted target held and guest memory never got is gone. The zeta's depth
  snapshot is now released with it (it was dropped without a release when a zeta was reallocated).
With both, PR #424's comparison order (depth FUNC reference, patches/upstream) gives the console's picture: the lit
pool under the lamp with the table's shadow on its right; the other order lights only a patch under the table.
The shadow maps (and the main zeta) are cleared with a ZSTENCIL_CLEAR_VALUE of 0: the game sets it once, for the
stencil-layer clear on a level's first frame (0x00BB56F0), and never writes the register again. On the console every
flip puts the RSX state back to its reset values (RPCS3: flip_command -> rsx_state::reset, ZSTENCIL_CLEAR_VALUE
0xFFFFFF00), so the later clears are to the far plane. The toolkit does not reset at a flip; the engine reading a 0
clear value as 1.0 stands in for that. The reset with an honest decode is PR #526
(https://github.com/sp00nznet/ps3recomp/pull/526); in a scripted run it gives the same Home frame, so it is not
carried here.

test_texture_layout: test_remap_depth_lanes (0xA900 and 0xAAE4 on all four depth formats; 24 failures without).
test_rsx_draw_engine: test_full_tables_evict_the_oldest -- 64 zetas, two frames, a zeta read as a texture: the 65th
takes the oldest one's slot and releases it, the read and the bound ones stay, after the old ones a full table of
this frame's zetas refuses; a 65th colour surface evicts the oldest, not the presented one (4 failures without the
eviction, 2 without the texture read counting as a use).
Scripted run (Home, CHAPTER ONE view, then a camera turn): the lamp shadows as on the console, nothing else changed
in the turn's frames; 3 surface and 1 zeta evictions logged by then. fps against 0012+0013 (2 runs each): standing
29.9-30.0 vs 30.0, turning 29.8-29.9 vs 30.0 (the game's cap; the shadowed lights now compare real depth).

Upstream: the crossbar part is PR #501 (https://github.com/sp00nznet/ps3recomp/pull/501); the table eviction is
PR #499's fourth commit (https://github.com/sp00nznet/ps3recomp/pull/499).

